        "title": "fix(ui): localize mobile pairing in Hindi and Russian",
        "body": "Related: #94672\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users running the Control UI in Hindi or Russian would see English copy in the mobile-pairing flow and six adjacent chat labels because those generated locale entries were recorded as fallbacks.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe missing Hindi and Russian strings are now localized, their generated metadata reports complete coverage, and focused regression tests prevent recorded fallbacks or untranslated mobile-pairing copy from shipping again. This is an AI-assisted maintainer follow-up to #94672.\n\n## User Impact\n\nHindi and Russian users now see localized setup-code, QR, pending-review, commentary, session, and expired-pairing messages. All 20 shipped Control UI locales report 1,438 of 1,438 translated keys with zero recorded fallbacks.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node --import tsx scripts/control-ui-i18n.ts check` — passed; 20/20 locales clean, zero fallbacks\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/control-ui-i18n.test.ts ui/src/i18n/test/translate.test.ts` — passed; 2 shards, 19 tests\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local ...` — clean; no accepted/actionable findings\n- `git diff --check` — passed\n",
